#: ../../../LibASTMatchersTutorial.md:533
msgid ""
"As a side note, it's not as trivial to test if two expressions are the same, "
"though Clang has already done the hard work for us by providing a way to "
"canonicalize expressions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LibASTMatchersTutorial.md:549
msgid ""
"This code relies on the comparison between two `llvm::FoldingSetNodeIDs`. As "
"the documentation for `Stmt::Profile()` indicates, the `Profile()` member "
"function builds a description of a node in the AST, based on its properties, "
"along with those of its children. `FoldingSetNodeID` then serves as a hash "
"we can use to compare expressions. We will need `areSameExpr` later. Before "
"you run the new code on the additional loops added to test-files/simple.cpp, "
"try to figure out which ones will be considered potentially convertible."
msgstr ""
